{"reference":"1 Kings 20","book":"1 Kings","chapter":20,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Wider Setting","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"An Assyrian inscription known as the Kurkh Monolith names Ahab as part of a coalition at Qarqar, an event not narrated in 1 Kings. It independently places an Israelite king within the regional politics of this broader period, though it does not confirm every detail or theological claim in the book.","verse_refs":[],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_kings_020_c5b68ec8456f57e96e71072a"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"inference"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}